<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11546" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄπαρνος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρνέομαι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>denying utterly,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. ἐστι μὴ νοσέειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					3.99
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				1.9
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				10
			</span></i>: c. gen., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. οὐδενὸς
			καθίστατο</span> she <i>denied</i> nothing, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				435
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>denied,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾇ . . οὐδὲν ἄπαρνον τελέθει</span>
			to whom nothing is <i>denied,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				1039
			</span></i> (lyr.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
